cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "torchbelief: differentiable belief functions and imprecise probabilities for PyTorch"
abstract: >-
  A PyTorch library for belief functions and imprecise probabilities. It fuses sources that
  disagree, finds out which one is wrong, and decides or abstains when the evidence does not
  single out an answer. Every operation is a batched, differentiable PyTorch op.
authors:
  - family-names: Sulc
    given-names: Antonin
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sulcantonin/torchbelief"
keywords:
  - belief functions
  - Dempster-Shafer theory
  - imprecise probability
  - uncertainty
  - sensor fusion
  - PyTorch
